WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:04.090
Ship goods from Rotterdam to
Yokohama via the Suez Canal,

2
00:00:04.140 --> 00:00:09.030
and the nominal distance is
about 11,200 nautical miles.

3
00:00:09.080 --> 00:00:12.950
Across the top of the
world, it's about 6,500.

4
00:00:13.000 --> 00:00:16.690
A shorter route could save
sailing time and fuel.

5
00:00:16.740 --> 00:00:21.110
So will melting ice turn the
Arctic into a new shipping highway?

6
00:00:21.160 --> 00:00:23.890
Will it replace Suez within a few years?

7
00:00:23.940 --> 00:00:28.350
In this mission, you'll calculate how
much shorter the Arctic route really is.

8
00:00:28.400 --> 00:00:31.630
Then you'll weigh how
hazards affect people:

9
00:00:31.680 --> 00:00:37.910
heat, disease, and 29.9 million
disaster displacements in 2025,

10
00:00:37.960 --> 00:00:40.530
counted as movements, not people.

11
00:00:40.580 --> 00:00:45.790
Your mission: decide whether melting ice
will make the Arctic a new shipping highway.
